      "text": "I wrote the answer to `answer.txt`. I worked it out by tracing the program by hand against the spec; I didn't run it.\n\nThe answer is:\n\n`6 7 12 16 7 101 200 1001 35 7 1 42 42 43 70 20 5 0 0 30 2001 1001`\n\nThe spec has no closures. A `fn` body sees only its own parameters and locals, and every other name reads the global. That is why `add5` picks up the global `n` (101, then 1001 after `SET n 1000`), not the `n` passed to `adder`. It is also why `times3 5` gives 35 (global `k` is still 7) and `times4 5` gives 0 (global `op` is 0, so the call yields 0).",
